{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520884-help-choosing-instrument","id":1520884,"title":"Help choosing instrument","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-18T08:20:07-07:00","id":1520884,"title":"Help choosing instrument","content":"A player is creating a \u201ctechnomancer\u201d mage, probably from hermetic House Thig. Her paradigm is basically focused into electromagnetism and ways to manipulate it to change reality. One of her ways to cast spells is to use electric components, like magnectic cores, copper coils and vibrating quartz that are present in several modern day stuff. <br /> However, the mage does not believe the objects are doing the effects (like a regular technomancer), she just use them as focus to mess with reality.<br /> <br /> She also has a golden ring, which is a wonder, that she wants to add into some of her effects.<br /> <br /> So, we don\u2019t know if she should take the instrument \u201cGems, stones and minerals&quot; that has in it\u2019s description its use in technology, or the instrument \u201cDevices and machines&quot;. Both are very vague...<br /> <br /> The first option seem to include way more than the character will use: which is only the electrically related minerals, like silver, copper, silicon, gold, etc. that are present in modern days devices. So no healing crystals nor rubies to cast magick, for example. This instrument could work, but she think it doesn\u2019t *feel* quite a technomancer this way.<br /> <br /> The second option is more on par with the mage concept, but I can\u2019t think of ways to include the golden ring wonder into it. I mean, gold has electrical properties and a ring could be considered a loop or single coil, but it\u2019s not quite a device nor machine is it?<br /> <br /> So, should I just include the ring into \u201cDevices and machines&quot; instrument for some reason, or should I suggest her to get \u201cGems, stones and minerals&quot; instead and go the broader way?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T08:23:36-07:00","id":1520886,"title":"","content":"Neither. Go with \u201celectrical conductors and insulators\u201d. That's a subset of \u201cgems, stones, and materials\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T09:04:20-07:00","id":1520888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520884-help-choosing-instrument?p=1520886#post1520886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither. Go with \u201celectrical conductors and insulators\u201d. That's a subset of \u201cgems, stones, and materials\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is? Is that raw? I like to follow raw as much as possible (even in an annoying way), but I think in this case there aren't much options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T09:07:18-07:00","id":1520889,"title":"","content":"It's not RAW; but the RAW Instruments are <i>examples</i>, not a comprehensive list. And that <i>is</i> RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T14:49:21-07:00","id":1520899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520884-help-choosing-instrument?p=1520889#post1520889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not RAW; but the RAW Instruments are <i>examples</i>, not a comprehensive list. And that <i>is</i> RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I see. The way you posted, it seemed that it was written somewhere and I thought I missed.<br /> <br /> Yeah, that list are examples, but I try to stick to it.<br /> <br /> But why did you made it a subset of Gem,stones and minerals? <br /> <br /> I might be wrong, but I see this instrument more as gemstones and crystals. While Devices and machines implies a bigger relation with technology?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure insulators should be there too. If a new instrument were to be created, I believe something on the like of &quot;Devices and electromagnetic conductors and components&quot; would fit entirely.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-18T15:15:12-07:00","id":1520903,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. As a former electrical engineer, my thought immediately went to \u201cmaterials that have useful electrical properties\u201d: conductors allow electricity to flow; insulators let you control where it flows; crystals vibrate at fixed frequencies which control alternating current, etc.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> what inspired me to this view was something I read about magical materials \u2014 that is, materials being used in spellcasting. The description classified them into \u201cconductors\u201d (which help the mystical energies flow) and \u201cinsulators\u201d (which keep those energies contained and not spreading to who knows where).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-18-2023, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-19T08:06:29-07:00","id":1520944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520884-help-choosing-instrument?p=1520903#post1520903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. As a former electrical engineer, my thought immediately went to \u201cmaterials that have useful electrical properties\u201d: conductors allow electricity to flow; insulators let you control where it flows; crystals vibrate at fixed frequencies which control alternating current, etc.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> what inspired me to this view was something I read about magical materials \u2014 that is, materials being used in spellcasting. The description classified them into \u201cconductors\u201d (which help the mystical energies flow) and \u201cinsulators\u201d (which keep those energies contained and not spreading to who knows where).</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. That is very good explanation. Well, I'm not sure the mage paradigm would deal with the containing aspect of it. I think it's more about the flow. Also, if I include both conductors and insulators, wouldn't that encompass practically...everything? <br /> <br /> Anyway, insulators could also be covered by the &quot;electromagnetic components&quot;, right? But then, conductors should be there too, so maybe a better name would be &quot;Devices and electromagnetic components&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T08:24:29-07:00","id":1521031,"title":"","content":"Also, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> , could you provide an example of the use of insulators to &quot;stop the flow&quot;? It would be cool to present that to the player, maybe we can work something out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T08:35:04-07:00","id":1521033,"title":"","content":"Drawing a circle of salt around a ritual space, so that if something goes wrong the backlash will remain confined within it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T10:41:54-07:00","id":1521041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520884-help-choosing-instrument?p=1521033#post1521033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Drawing a circle of salt around a ritual space, so that if something goes wrong the backlash will remain confined within it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case the salt is the insulator, right? Would that mean that the mage can use practically everything (any object), since most things are either good or bad at conducting electricity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T10:58:51-07:00","id":1521044,"title":"","content":"Salt as an insulator for mystical energies, yes. <br /> <br /> In terms of using things as electrical conductors and insulators: I'd limit the materials to those that are <i>exceptionally</i> good or bad at conducting electricity. Metals, almost by definition, are good conductors; plastics tend to be good insulators. That's why wires are strands of metal encased in plastic. <br /> <br /> And crystals aren't so much about conducting electricity as they're about regulating its properties. In that regard, they're similar to semiconductors: diodes, transistors, and so on: a semiconductor is a material that's been designed to conduct in certain circumstances and to insulate in others, letting them act as switches and relays that don't do much determine how much or how little electricity flows, but <i>when</i> and <i>where</i> it flows. <br /> <br /> And remember that the Focus in question isn't actually based on the electrical properties of the materials; it's based on what those materials symbolize. So materials that have been traditionally associated with electricity will work better as Instruments than materials that <i>don't </i>have that association.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T12:56:23-07:00","id":1521055,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this is helpful in your case, but maybe it can spark some ideas: when I was playing Tremere, the player of my apprentice had a technomancer character while I played an oldschool hermetic alchemist. What we did for her research was to create a table of correspondences that aimed to integrate circuitry components into the classic hermetic system, like so:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td width=\"55\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Planet</b></td> <td width=\"56\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Metal</b></td> <td width=\"64\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Mineral</b></td> <td width=\"102\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 4px\"><b>Component</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"></tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"tex